RBOR-1#1 Warning
RAMB output registers  
RAMB mlp_inst/memory_inst/bias_bram_reg output DOB (5) is connected to asynchronous registers, if you use synchronous controls you will get better results both in area and delay (RAMB has synchronous registers built in).
Related violations: <none>

REQP-1839#1 Warning
RAMB36 async control check  
The RAMB36E1 mlp_inst/memory_inst/input_bram_reg has an input control pin mlp_inst/memory_inst/input_bram_reg/ADDRARDADDR[10] (net: mlp_inst/memory_inst/input_addr[7]) which is driven by a register (FSM_onehot_state_reg[3]) that has an active asychronous set or reset. This may cause corruption of the memory contents and/or read values when the set/reset is asserted and is not analyzed by the default static timing analysis. It is suggested to eliminate the use of a set/reset to registers driving this RAMB pin or else use a synchronous reset in which the assertion of the reset is timed by default.
Related violations: <none>

